ute_common_abstract_core
====================
Core functionality of Abstract Libraries:
* `stack` - basic stack operations
* `scope` - automated releasing of resources used inside testcase/testsuite scope; release is made when scope ends
* `logger` - logging module configuration, logging decorators (to simplify building logging systems)
* `aliases registry` - singleton that holds mapping between alias-name and object stored inside registry
* `NetworkElementIdentification` - class allowing to identify same NetworkElem based on different identification
* `NetworkElementFactory` - factory returning recipe "how to build specific variant of NetworkElem" - may be input for 'instance loader'
* `NetworkElementValidator` - uniform validation of variant-specific-elements related to NetworkElem (like variant-specific-id of UE)
* `instance loader` - factory that allows object creation based on package-class-name and constructor parameters (instead of eval)
* `singleton` - metaclass to create classes that should follow Singleton Design Pattern
* `message query language` - to allow building composed queries for message content
* `config` - common configuration used by multiple abstract libraries
* `device_pool` - base classes for building specific device pools in more efficient way
* `plugin system` - allows external python packages to register their implementation(s) of device-poo
* `device_characteristics` - base class for building specific device characteristics
* `robot_redirecting_handler` - handler for redirecting log-records from python subthreads to RobotFramework logger
* `robot_console_redirecting_handler` - handler for redirecting log-records to RobotFramework console. Configurable via UTE_UE_CONSOLE_LOG_CONFIG environment variable.


Requirements
============
* PyYAML >= 3.11
* ply >= 3.4
* funcsigs >= 1.0.2
* mock >= 2.0.0
* robotframework >= 3.0.4
* six >= 1.10.0
